questions.question:
The four rules below all set the colour of the same button.
```html
<button class="important" id="confirm">Delete Account</button>
```
```css
button { color: blue; }
.important { color: red; }
#confirm { color: green; }
button.important { color: orange; }
```
(a) What colour is the button text, and how does the browser choose between the four rules?
(b) The student adds !important to the first rule. What colour is the text now?
(c) Why does routinely using !important cause problems? Describe what a developer should usually do when a rule is not taking effect.
